  "articleBody": "Ready to dive into a home renovation? Getting started on the right foot makes all the difference! Here’s a quick checklist to help you prepare:\n\n1. **Define Your Scope & Budget:** Before you even talk to a contractor, have a clear idea of what you want done and how much you're willing to spend. This helps everyone stay on the same page.\n2. **Verify Credentials:** Always check for current licensing and general liability insurance. This protects you and ensures you're working with a legitimate business, like HH Remodeling LLC, an Aurora-based, BBB Accredited company.\n3. **Gather References:** Ask for references, especially from past residential projects similar to yours. A good contractor will be happy to provide them, and it’s smart to follow up.\n4. **Review the Bid & Contract:** Get a detailed, written bid that outlines everything included and, just as importantly, what’s *excluded*. Make sure the payment schedule is clear and fair.\n5. **Confirm Permits & Inspections:** Understand who is responsible for obtaining all necessary permits and coordinating inspections. This is crucial for compliance and avoiding delays.\n6. **Discuss Communication:** Establish how you'll communicate throughout the project—who to contact, how often, and through what method. Open communication prevents misunderstandings.\n7. **Ask About Warranties:** Inquire about any workmanship guarantees or warranties. This gives you peace of mind long after the project is complete. \n\nBy checking these off, you'll be well-prepared to kick off your renovation with confidence.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}